<div class="back-to-top" data-back-to-top>
  {% comment %}
    Swapped to an anchor link pointing to the MainContent ID we put in theme.liquid.
    This naturally shifts screen reader and keyboard focus back to the top of the site's content.
  {% endcomment %}
  <a
    href="#top-back"
    class="back-to-top__button global-button global-button--{{ settings.back_to_top_button_style }}"
    aria-label="Back to top" role="button" tabindex="0"
  >
    {% comment %} 
      We wrap the labels in aria-hidden="true" so screen readers ignore 
      the visual toggle and only read the clean fallback aria-label above.
    {% endcomment %}
    <span aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="back-to-top__desktop-label-wrapper">
        <span
          class="
            back-to-top__button-label
            back-to-top__button-label--desktop
          "
        >
          {{- 'general.back_to_top_button.desktop_button_label' | t -}}
        </span>
      </span>

      <span
        class="
          back-to-top__button-label
          back-to-top__button-label--mobile
        "
      >
        {{- 'general.back_to_top_button.mobile_button_label' | t -}}
      </span>
    </span>

    {% comment %} 
      Icons should always be hidden from screen readers. 
      If you have an up arrow icon in your theme, change the class below!
    {% endcomment %}
    <span class="icon-down-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </a>
</div>